-- the body of a view that runs as another user can be rewritten only with SET DEFINER on that user
reads secret     ACCESS_DENIED
on cluster       ACCESS_DENIED
reads only src   ACCESS_DENIED
row policy       ACCESS_DENIED
after the grant  accepted
-- a SQL SECURITY NONE body runs unchecked, so rewriting it needs ALLOW SQL SECURITY NONE
security none    ACCESS_DENIED
after the grant  accepted
-- a MODIFY SQL SECURITY in the same statement decides what the body runs as, so the old one
-- must not be what gets authorized
take over        accepted
hand to other    ACCESS_DENIED
-- a definer named <user>:definer is a real user unless <user> is ephemeral
real, base grant ACCESS_DENIED
real, own view   accepted
cluster no view  UNKNOWN_TABLE on the initiator
-- no data leaked: none of the denied bodies was stored
rows, leaked     1	0
